From 559da17172b427274ec06eadd05ff83b815dbee6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:03:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(setup): part-in-spindle mode and table tool stations
 on a mill

A mill setup can hold the part in its spindle (a collet) with lathe tools
on the table. SetupDef::part_in_spindle states the stock's length offset
register, the collet stick-out and outer diameter, and the table
stations: each tool's own 1-based work offset, approach side (-X/+X) and
spindle direction (M3/M4). Two tools never share one work offset.

The undoable SetPartInSpindle and SetTableStation commands and the MCP
tools set_part_in_spindle and set_table_station configure it; get_job
shows it; the project file keeps it as an additive key, and the loader
refuses a record the commands would refuse.

In the mode, the family door admits turning work and an axial Drill and
refuses milling and cross holes by name; the setup's work is generated
as a lathe's (the axial door and the spindle law hold), and the lathe
field eye simulates it. The collet's workholding max rpm is required and
enforced; with no post section for table stations yet, the post is
refused by name.

Fixes #3406

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
